# Pass Only What a Method Needs

**Rule:** When writing a helper method, declare parameters for exactly the data it uses (e.g. `List<TicketEntity> tickets`) instead of accepting the whole Bloc/Cubit `State` and reaching into its fields. Passing the entire `State` couples the method to the full state shape, hurts reuse and testability, and hides what the method actually needs. If another field is required, read it directly from `context.read<Cubit>().state` inside the method or add that specific parameter.

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
void _syncTabs(TicketDetailState state) {
  final tickets = state.tickets;
  if (tickets.isEmpty) return;
}

_syncTabs(context.read<TicketDetailCubit>().state);
```

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
void _syncTabs(List<TicketEntity> tickets) {
  if (tickets.isEmpty) return;
  final int? selectedId =
      context.read<TicketDetailCubit>().state.selectedTicketId;
}

_syncTabs(context.read<TicketDetailCubit>().state.tickets);
```
